    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.35.3</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:40:30 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23503</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.35.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><p><strong>Ducks are Open or Closed.</strong></p><ul><li>"Off duty" is now Closed and "On duty" is now Open, everywhere: the roster, the Dashboard, search and the @ list. A closed Duck says "Closed 3d ago" and has Reopen.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.2</h4><p><strong>Ducklings that died with a restart stop showing as running.</strong></p><ul><li>When a duck's session restarts, a duckling it had running ends with it. Squeak now shows that duckling as stopped instead of "1 duckling running" forever, and it leaves the bar after ten minutes like any finished one.</li><li>A duckling whose state is unknown shows how long it really ran, not "0s".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.1</h4><p><strong>A tidier Pond list and image paste that always answers.</strong></p><ul><li>All · Shared · Not shared now lives in the filter menu next to Ponds instead of its own row. The filter icon darkens while a filter is on.</li><li>Pasting or dropping an image into a duck's chat or a new duck never silently does nothing: it attaches, or says under the box why it can't. Images copied from Finder, browsers and spreadsheets paste more reliably.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
